{"name":"Pink Pandora","hex":"#e1c5c9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"pandora","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any fish of the genus Pagellus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pandora"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pandora","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Pandora was the first human woman, created by Hephaestus on the instructions of Zeus. As Hesiod related it, each deity cooperated by giving her unique gifts. Her other name—inscribed against her figure on a white-ground kylix in the British Museum—is Anesidora."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Abel-josef-1764-1818-austria-prometheus-merkur-und-die-pand.jpg/330px-Abel-josef-1764-1818-austria-prometheus-merkur-und-die-pand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandora","wikidata":"Q131346"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Pandora_-_John_William_Waterhouse.jpg/500px-Pandora_-_John_William_Waterhouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki